<title>FRANCE: Club Med sells cruise ship for $45 mln.</title>
<headline>Club Med sells cruise ship for $45 mln.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Resorts group Club Mediterranee said on Wednesday its jointly-owned Services et Transports Cruise Lines has agreed the sale of the Club Med 1 cruise liner for $45 million to Carnival Corp, with delivery set for March 1998.</p>
<p>Club Med will continue to use the cruise ship under existing conditions until the delivery date, when Club Med 2 will take over its cruises in the Mediterranean and Caribbean.</p>
<p>Services et Transports Cruise Lines is owned by Club Med and Services et Transports, a shipping company based in the port city of Le Havre.</p>
</text>
